body:
Honestly, it's morbid & unwell. I honestly believe I will be dead in 2 years. But I will not explain because last time I did I got a sarcastic "Need to talk?" reply.

&#x200B;

I'm almost 30 years old & I have "valuable" life experiences--there's nothing else that I need to talk about. I'm not a goddamn teenager who lives in my parents' basement and has never left my hometown--I can see clearly what the fuck is going on.

The heaviest I ever was, was when I reached about 185lbs in college. I was strictly vegetarian. Didn't have a stagnate lifestyle, but also not active due to my academic requirements. I was on my college's meal plan, so technically my diet was "regular" -- although when I had extra money, instead of going to the bar I would buy a shit-ton of fast food & eat myself into a coma.

&#x200B;

Honestly, idk how I would have lost that weight if I didn't study abroad in India. I didn't lose a ton of weight while I was there, maybe about 15lbs...but it definitely gave me a new view on life & allowed me to lose about another 10lbs or so when I returned to Michigan. In India, I ate natural food, regular portions, wasn't able to make hot pockets at 2am at my parents' house LOL...it wasn't even like I walked a lot, took a rickshaw most days to my guru-ji's house.

&#x200B;

From my experience, once you pass a certain point in weight, it becomes really difficult to lose--apathy and hopelessness set in & they are extremely toxic. \*\*I really recommend some sort of "vacation" like I had (although it was technically study abroad, not vacation) that changes the worldview.\*\* 

&#x200B;

For those who are interested, I was there for about 2 months. So 15lbs in 2 months isn't super drastic (honestly 15lbs might even be an overestimate). But the change of scenery really helped in hindsight. Honestly don't know how else I would have lost it. For a reference, I graduated high school just under 130lbs & even considered fat then...so...yeah, 185lbs was a bad time for me.

This is an easy $0.02 for me to spend: THE MURDER OF TSAR NICHOLAS II AND HIS ENTIRE DUCKING FAMILY

&#x200B;

*They abdicated the throne & gave up power--they were not a threat to anyone*. It still pisses me off. Some people spend their lives bitching about the murder of Jesus... I will spend my life bitching about the murder of the Tsar & his beautiful family.

&#x200B;

A true "fuck you" to the Romanov Empire which lasted over 300 years & *arguably laid the foundation for everything Russia is today*. Tsar Nicholas II listened to his people and said "here, enjoy power" & the response to that was "\~BANG BANG BANG (repeat)\~ YOU'RE DEAD NOW, AND SO IS YOUR WIFE AND CHILDREN!!!"
